{"title":"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 31","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The rails on a railroad are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet long. As the train passes over the point where the rails are joined, there is an audible click. \nThe speed of the train in miles per hour is approximately the number of clicks heard in: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a74b24573e7f2494d1ab76dff265106da67a342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 20\\text{ seconds} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\text{ minutes} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 1\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ minutes}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 5\\text{ minutes}\\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"543\" height=\"55\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the speed of the train in miles per hour. By dimensional analysis, the speed in clicks per minute is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/11869c1a0d85c96ed4f9147887e0748105d9e198.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{x\\text{ mi}}{1\\text{ hr}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1\\text{ hr}}{60\\text{ min}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{5280\\text{ ft}}{1\\text{ mi}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1\\text{ click}}{30\\text{ ft}}\\right)=\\frac{5280x\\text{ click}}{1800\\text{ min}} = \\frac{44}{15}x \\text{ click}/\\text{min} \\approx 3x\\text{ click}/\\text{min}\\]\" width=\"674\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> clicks are heard per minute. So approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> clicks are heard per <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> minute, that is, approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> clicks are heard per <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8adef399cb169c8d14156c273baaca7bdb2ef09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 20\\text{ seconds}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"125\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"backg